# What Fedora calls the same things.
#
# The names differ more than they look. Debian's mail-transport-agent
# is Fedora's MTA; Debian's libgl1 is Fedora's mesa-libGL. A profile
# that named either directly would work on exactly one of them.

Capability: web-browser
Resolves-To: firefox | chromium | epiphany

Capability: terminal-emulator
Resolves-To: foot | alacritty | kitty | konsole | gnome-terminal | xterm

Capability: file-manager
Resolves-To: dolphin | nautilus | thunar

Capability: text-editor
Resolves-To: kate | gedit | nano

Capability: document-viewer
Resolves-To: okular | evince

Capability: image-viewer
Resolves-To: gwenview | eog

Capability: word-processor
Resolves-To: libreoffice-writer | abiword

Capability: spreadsheet
Resolves-To: libreoffice-calc | gnumeric

Capability: mail-transport-agent
Resolves-To: MTA | smtpdaemon | postfix | msmtp

Capability: audio-server
Resolves-To: pipewire | pulseaudio

Capability: vulkan-driver
Resolves-To: mesa-vulkan-drivers | nvidia-driver-libs

Capability: opengl
Resolves-To: mesa-libGL

Capability: firewall
Resolves-To: firewalld | nftables | iptables

Capability: time-sync
Resolves-To: chrony | systemd-timesyncd

Capability: ssh-server
Resolves-To: openssh-server

Capability: compiler-toolchain
Resolves-To: gcc-c++ | gcc

Capability: vpn-client
Resolves-To: wireguard-tools

Capability: steam
Resolves-To: steam

Capability: init
Resolves-To: systemd

Capability: c-library
Resolves-To: glibc | musl-libc

Capability: core-utilities
Resolves-To: coreutils

Capability: package-manager
Resolves-To: dnf5 | dnf | rpm

Capability: archiver
Resolves-To: tar

Capability: desktop-session
Resolves-To: plasma-workspace | gnome-shell | xfce4-session

Capability: display-manager
Resolves-To: sddm | gdm | lightdm

Capability: archive-manager
Resolves-To: ark | file-roller | xarchiver

Capability: system-settings
Resolves-To: plasma-systemsettings | gnome-control-center

# gnome-shell is last on purpose. Since GNOME 42 the screenshot
# tool is part of the shell rather than a package of its own, so
# a machine can have the capability with nothing named after it
# installed. Aliases go stale this way: ecosystems absorb tools
# into larger packages, and the alias still names the tool.
Capability: screenshot-tool
Resolves-To: spectacle | flameshot | gnome-screenshot | gnome-shell

Capability: lightweight-session
Resolves-To: openbox | i3 | fluxbox | xfce4-session

Capability: compositor-effects
Resolves-To: kwin-wayland | kwin-x11 | mutter

Capability: icon-theme
Resolves-To: breeze-icon-theme | adwaita-icon-theme | papirus-icon-theme

Capability: cursor-theme
Resolves-To: breeze-cursor-theme | adwaita-cursor-theme

Capability: font-collection
Resolves-To: google-noto-fonts-common | dejavu-fonts-all | liberation-fonts

Capability: network-applet
Resolves-To: plasma-nm | network-manager-applet

Capability: volume-applet
Resolves-To: plasma-pa | pavucontrol

Capability: desktop-portal
Resolves-To: xdg-desktop-portal-kde | xdg-desktop-portal-gnome | xdg-desktop-portal-gtk

Capability: window-manager
Resolves-To: sway | hyprland | i3 | bspwm | dwm | river

Capability: status-bar
Resolves-To: waybar | polybar | i3status

Capability: application-launcher
Resolves-To: fuzzel | rofi | wofi | dmenu | bemenu

Capability: notification-daemon
Resolves-To: mako | dunst

Capability: screen-locker
Resolves-To: swaylock | i3lock | xsecurelock

Capability: wallpaper-setter
Resolves-To: swaybg | feh | nitrogen

Capability: compositor
Resolves-To: picom | xcompmgr

Capability: modern-shell
Resolves-To: zsh | fish

Capability: terminal-multiplexer
Resolves-To: tmux | zellij | screen

Capability: fuzzy-finder
Resolves-To: fzf | skim
